1 Introduction
**************

The ‘isomd5sum’ package provides four command-line tools for embedding
and verifying integrity checksums in ISO 9660 disc images.  These
checksums are stored in the application data area of the ISO 9660
Primary Volume Descriptor, a region unused by the standard
specification.  This means the checksum can be verified directly from
the ‘.iso’ file or from physical media without any separate checksum
file.

1.1 Tools
=========

‘implantisomd5’
     Embeds an MD5 checksum into an ISO 9660 image.

‘checkisomd5’
     Reads and optionally verifies the MD5 checksum embedded by
     ‘implantisomd5’.

‘implantisosha’
     Embeds a SHA-256 checksum into an ISO 9660 image.  This is the
     preferred tool for new images because SHA-256 is stronger than MD5.

‘checkisosha’
     Reads and optionally verifies a SHA-256 or MD5 checksum.  Because
     it understands both algorithm types it can be used as a single tool
     for verifying any image produced by either implant command.

1.2 Checksum Storage
====================

The checksum data is stored as a null-terminated ASCII string starting
at byte offset 883 of the ISO 9660 Primary Volume Descriptor.  The
string contains key-value pairs including the algorithm type, the hex
checksum, and the number of sectors covered.


