2 implantisomd5
***************

2.1 Synopsis
============

     implantisomd5 [OPTIONS] ISOFILE

2.2 Description
===============

‘implantisomd5’ embeds an MD5 checksum into the application data area of
the ISO 9660 Primary Volume Descriptor of ISOFILE.  The image must be a
valid ISO 9660 file.

   For new images, consider using ‘implantisosha’ instead, which embeds
a SHA-256 checksum and is considered more secure.

2.3 Options
===========

‘--force’
     Overwrite any existing checksum already embedded in the image.
     Without this option, ‘implantisomd5’ will refuse to modify an image
     that already contains a checksum.

‘--supported-iso’
     Mark the image as targeted at “supported” media (e.g., a pressed
     CD).  On Red Hat-based Anaconda installers, this flag bypasses the
     interactive prompt that asks the user to verify the disc.

2.4 Exit Status
===============

0
     The checksum was implanted successfully.
1
     An error occurred.  Typical causes include the file not being
     found, the file not being a valid ISO 9660 image, or an existing
     checksum being present without ‘--force’.


