3 checkisomd5
*************

3.1 Synopsis
============

     checkisomd5 [OPTIONS] {ISOFILE | DEVICE}

3.2 Description
===============

‘checkisomd5’ reads the MD5 checksum embedded in ISOFILE (or block
DEVICE) by ‘implantisomd5’ and optionally recomputes the checksum to
verify the image's integrity.

   The check can be aborted by pressing the <Esc> key.

3.3 Options
===========

‘--md5sumonly’
     Do not verify the image.  Instead, print human-readable information
     about the embedded checksum (algorithm, value, and sectors covered)
     then exit.

‘--verbose’
     Print a human-readable progress report as the image is read and
     verified.  Without this option, no output is produced unless an
     error occurs.

‘--gauge’
     Print a stream of numbers from 0 to 100 representing verification
     progress.  This is suitable for piping into ‘dialog --gauge’ to
     provide a user-facing progress bar.

3.4 Exit Status
===============

0
     The embedded checksum matches the image (verification passed).
1
     The checksum is missing, or the recomputed checksum does not match
     (verification failed).
2
     The check was aborted by the user.


