4 implantisosha
***************

4.1 Synopsis
============

     implantisosha [OPTIONS] ISOFILE

4.2 Description
===============

‘implantisosha’ embeds a SHA-256 checksum into the application data area
of the ISO 9660 Primary Volume Descriptor of ISOFILE.  SHA-256 provides
stronger integrity guarantees than MD5 and is the recommended algorithm
for new images.

   Images produced by ‘implantisosha’ can be verified by both
‘checkisosha’ and ‘checkisomd5’.

4.3 Options
===========

‘--force’
     Overwrite any existing checksum already embedded in the image.

‘--supported-iso’
     Mark the image as targeted at supported media.  On Red Hat-based
     Anaconda installers this bypasses the interactive disc-check
     prompt.

4.4 Exit Status
===============

0
     The checksum was implanted successfully.
1
     An error occurred.


