5 checkisosha
*************

5.1 Synopsis
============

     checkisosha [OPTIONS] {ISOFILE | DEVICE}

5.2 Description
===============

‘checkisosha’ reads and optionally verifies a SHA-256 or MD5 checksum
embedded in ISOFILE (or block DEVICE).  It supports checksums produced
by both ‘implantisosha’ and ‘implantisomd5’, making it suitable as a
single verification tool for any isomd5sum-annotated image.

   The check can be aborted by pressing the <Esc> key.

5.3 Options
===========

‘--md5sumonly’
     Do not verify the image.  Instead, print human-readable information
     about the embedded checksum then exit.

‘--verbose’
     Print a human-readable progress report as the image is verified.

‘--gauge’
     Print a stream of numbers from 0 to 100 representing verification
     progress, suitable for piping into ‘dialog --gauge’.

5.4 Exit Status
===============

0
     Verification passed.
1
     The checksum is missing or does not match.
2
     The check was aborted by the user.


